# THE CANISTER, STRAIGHT DOWN. The tank (a body island of 496 vertices) and its two end caps, ringed by two straps and
# sitting over a valve pipe at its rear underside. No line out of it is clear of the gun -- back is the grip and hose,
# forward the heat shield, up the barrel -- so it drops straight down, the least in the way: it passes through the
# straps' lower loops and the top of the rear valve pipe (z -3.25, x -12.6..-10.2) as it goes. Distance: its top (z 4.67)
# down past the straps' bottoms (z -8.55), plus 0.4.
part canister
  role    = feed
  subject = magazine
  take    = no          # out by its button, in by the hand carrying one
  surface = canister
  # Its underside, the lowest half unit of it: the hand takes it from below.
  grab       = 0.38, -0.46, -8.52
  grabradius = 3.0
  dof
    kind     = slide
    axis     = 0, 0, -1
    distance = 13.62
    detach   = 0.9
  end
end

# THE TRIGGER: a hinge in the donor, 14.98 degrees about (0, 1, 0) through its pin, fit 0.009 (tools/card_skeleton.py at
# frame 3; +14.98 lands it, -14.98 misses by 1.949). The pin as the re-origin moved it.
part trigger
  role    = trigger
  surface = trigger
  dof
    kind    = hinge
    axis    = 0, 1, 0
    degrees = 14.98
    pivot   = -21.91, -0.47, 1.34
  end
end

# THE DONOR'S PILOT FLAME: an untextured cone on the side igniter's tip (centroid 55.50, 3.53, 0.19). Hidden, as the
# Flamer's, while RS_Ballistics draws the live one.
part pilotflame
  role    = hidden
  surface = pilotflame
end

# THE OTHER HAND ON THE BARREL: the top tube's underside just ahead of the heat shield (x 25.55..27.44, z 6.02), before
# the tube bends down to the shroud. The point is MEASURED; that the hand goes there is an ESTIMATE.
part support
  role    = support
  subject = support
  grab       = 26.68, -0.47, 6.02
  grabradius = 3.0
end
